    marker_positions: (r0-1,c0-1), (r0-1,c1+1), (r1+1,c0-1), (r1+1,c1+1)
    placement: marker-expanded zones (bbox+1 on each side) must not overlap each other or exceed grid bounds
  other_pixels: none; only GREY rectangles and their 4 markers on BLACK background
  output:
    markers erased to BLACK
    each GREY rect split into 4 equal quadrants recolored by corresponding corner marker
    TL-quadrant=TL-marker, TR-quadrant=TR-marker, BL-quadrant=BL-marker, BR-quadrant=BR-marker

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (simple enough constraints)
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size H=W from 10-20 (even values convenient)
    2. Pick number of rectangles N from 1-3
    3. For each rectangle, pick even side length S from {2,4,6}
    4. Place rectangles one at a time; each needs an (S+2)x(S+2) clear zone for rect+markers; reject placements that overlap previously placed zones or exceed grid bounds
    5. For each rectangle, pick 4 distinct colors from {1,2,3,4,6,7,8,9} (all non-BLACK, non-GREY) for TL/TR/BL/BR markers
    6. Fill the SxS region with GREY, place 4 marker pixels at diagonal corners
    7. All remaining cells stay BLACK
